     I suspect that when you attempted to revert to unmodified
sources, you neglected to remove changes from the `util' subdirectory.
As someone else mentioned, nethack's util/lev*.* code doesn't reference
those two symbols.  But the suggestion to look for compiler patches
seems way off base; nethack has lots of other symbols which are close
to those, so it looks very much like something introduced by a source
patch.  (You might eventually end up needing compiler patches *anyway*,
but not for this.)

     My guess is that a patch has modified lev_comp.y but that you
haven't rebuilt lev_yacc.c with yacc or byacc or bison, so you are
building with only part of one of those patches in place.  I wouldn't
be surprised if the nethackW build projects are relying on copying
the pre-generated lev_yacc.c from the sys/share/ directory and that
the source patch you applied didn't bother updating that file to keep
it in synch with util/lev_comp.y.


